# Opaque wrapper of the program's `malloc_message` hook, a function pointer.
Hook	function pointer	Kani
# The C caller hands over the block it frees under the entry point's contract.
axiom_c_call	C-program contract	none (assumption)
# The two volatile reads of the hook slots the C program writes: Kani runs
# the body on every pair of hook values (none or one of two functions);
# what the program stores there, and when, is its contract (C1).
message_hook	UnsafeCell/volatile/transmute	Kani	discharged on premises (Kani: api::jemalloc::kani_hook::message_hook_picks_first_set; premises: C1 (the program stores only null or a hook function in the two slots, and never while the volatile reads run))	contract 3679688309, body 4059375492
# The report's call of the program's `malloc_message` hook: Kani runs the
# body on a recording hook and any buffer holding a NUL; what the program
# stores in the slots is its contract (C1), and what the hook does once
# called is its contract too (C3).
call_hook	function pointer	Kani	discharged on premises (Kani: api::jemalloc::kani_hook::call_hook_calls_once; premises: C1 (the program stores only null or a hook function in the two slots), C3 (the program's hook keeps the C allocation contract))	contract 4272715841, body 924183077
